## Section: Verbs

<section id="verbs">
<purpose>Verb conjugation patterns - how endings show who is doing the action</purpose>

### Start Here: είμαι (to be)

<insight title="Start Here: είμαι (to be)" icon="Star">
The most common Greek verb. Memorize it first. You'll use it in every conversation.

| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | είμαι (I am) | είμαστε (we are) |
| 2nd | είσαι (you are) | είστε (you are) |
| 3rd | είναι (he/she/it is) | είναι (they are) |

<note>3rd person singular and plural are identical: είναι</note>
</insight>

### The Power of Patterns

<alert variant="info">
Learn just **3 ending patterns** and you can conjugate thousands of verbs. The endings tell you WHO is doing the action.
</alert>

### Negation

<note>
**Negation:** Add δεν before the verb: Δεν μιλάω (I don't speak)
</note>

### Pattern Identifier

<identifier title="Which Pattern?" colour="honey">
Look at the verb's dictionary form (1st person singular):

| Ending | Pattern | Examples |
|--------|---------|----------|
| -ω | Active | κάνω, θέλω |
| -άω/-ώ | Contracted | μιλάω, αγαπάω |
| -μαι | Deponent | έρχομαι, θυμάμαι |
</identifier>

### Pattern 1: Active (-ω)

<pattern id="active" colour="ocean" badge="Learn First">
<header>
Active -ω Verbs
<ending>-ω</ending>
<description>The most common pattern. Covers thousands of verbs.</description>
</header>

<paradigm stem="κάν" infinitive="κάνω" meaning="to do/make">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | κάν**ω** | κάν**ουμε** |
| 2nd | κάν**εις** | κάν**ετε** |
| 3rd | κάν**ει** | κάν**ουν(ε)** |
</paradigm>

<same-pattern>
- θέλω (to want)
- βλέπω (to see)
- γράφω (to write)
- διαβάζω (to read)
- τρώω (to eat)
- πίνω (to drink)
- ξέρω (to know)
</same-pattern>

<in-context>
| Greek | English | Form |
|-------|---------|------|
| Τι κάνεις; | How are you? | -εις |
| Κάνει κρύο. | It's cold. | -ει |
| Κάνουμε διάλειμμα. | We're taking a break. | -ουμε |
</in-context>
</pattern>

### Pattern 2: Contracted (-άω/-ώ)

<pattern id="contracted" colour="terracotta">
<header>
Contracted -άω/-ώ Verbs
<ending>-άω/-ώ</ending>
<description>Verbs with α before the ending. The α contracts in some forms.</description>
</header>

<paradigm stem="μιλ" infinitive="μιλάω" meaning="to speak">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | μιλ**άω/ώ** | μιλ**άμε** |
| 2nd | μιλ**άς** | μιλ**άτε** |
| 3rd | μιλ**άει/ά** | μιλ**άνε/ούν(ε)** |
</paradigm>

<same-pattern>
- αγαπάω (to love)
- ρωτάω (to ask)
- περπατάω (to walk)
- γελάω (to laugh)
- κοιτάω (to look at)
</same-pattern>

<in-context>
| Greek | English | Form |
|-------|---------|------|
| Μιλάς ελληνικά; | Do you speak Greek? | -άς |
| Δεν μιλάμε πολύ. | We don't speak much. | -άμε |
</in-context>
</pattern>

### Pattern 3: Deponent (-μαι)

<pattern id="deponent" colour="olive">
<header>
Deponent Verbs (-μαι)
<ending>-μαι</ending>
<description>Passive form but active meaning. Two sub-patterns mirror the active ones.</description>
</header>

<sub-pattern type="-ομαι" canonical="έρχομαι" meaning="to come">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | έρχ**ομαι** | ερχ**όμαστε** |
| 2nd | έρχ**εσαι** | έρχ**εστε** |
| 3rd | έρχ**εται** | έρχ**ονται** |
</sub-pattern>

<sub-pattern type="-άμαι" canonical="θυμάμαι" meaning="to remember">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | θυμ**άμαι** | θυμ**όμαστε** |
| 2nd | θυμ**άσαι** | θυμ**άστε** |
| 3rd | θυμ**άται** | θυμ**ούνται** |
</sub-pattern>

<same-pattern>
- κοιμάμαι (to sleep)
- φοβάμαι (to be afraid)
- χρειάζομαι (to need)
- στέκομαι (to stand)
</same-pattern>

<in-context>
| Greek | English | Form |
|-------|---------|------|
| Έρχομαι αύριο. | I'm coming tomorrow. | -ομαι |
| Πότε έρχεσαι; | When are you coming? | -εσαι |
| Δεν θυμάμαι. | I don't remember. | -άμαι |
</in-context>
</pattern>

### Other Irregular Verbs

<irregulars colour="honey">
These common verbs don't follow patterns. Learn through frequent exposure.

<verb infinitive="έχω" meaning="to have">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | έχω | έχουμε |
| 2nd | έχεις | έχετε |
| 3rd | έχει | έχουν |
</verb>

<verb infinitive="λέω" meaning="to say">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | λέω | λέμε |
| 2nd | λες | λέτε |
| 3rd | λέει | λένε |
</verb>

<verb infinitive="πάω" meaning="to go">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | πάω | πάμε |
| 2nd | πας | πάτε |
| 3rd | πάει | πάνε |
</verb>

<verb infinitive="τρώω" meaning="to eat">
| Person | Singular | Plural |
|--------|----------|--------|
| 1st | τρώω | τρώμε |
| 2nd | τρως | τρώτε |
| 3rd | τρώει | τρώνε |
<note>Follows active pattern but with some irregular forms</note>
</verb>
</irregulars>

